pull.body:
This PR kills 3 mutants from https://mutanthub.space/mutants in validation.cpp 
I batched them together because the assertions are within the same test

Mutants killed:

Mutant 4388: validation.cpp ActivateBestChains, && → ||

```diff
@@ -6482,7 +6482,7 @@ util::Result<void> ChainstateManager::ActivateBestChains()
         for (const auto& chainstate : m_chainstates) {
-            if (chainstate && chainstate->m_assumeutxo != Assumeutxo::INVALID && !chainstate->m_target_utxohash) {
+            if (chainstate || chainstate->m_assumeutxo != Assumeutxo::INVALID && !chainstate->m_target_utxohash) {
                 chainstates.push_back(chainstate.get());
```

Mutant 4385: validation.cpp GetPruneRange, + 1 → - 1

```diff
@@ -6447,7 +6447,7 @@ std::pair<int, int> Chainstate::GetPruneRange(int last_height_can_prune) const
-        prune_start = Assert(SnapshotBase())->nHeight + 1;
+        prune_start = Assert(SnapshotBase())->nHeight - 1;
```

Mutant 4386: validation.cpp GetPruneRange, - → + MIN_BLOCKS_TO_KEEP

```diff
@@ -6451,7 +6451,7 @@ std::pair<int, int> Chainstate::GetPruneRange(int last_height_can_prune) const
     int max_prune = std::max<int>(
-        0, m_chain.Height() - static_cast<int>(MIN_BLOCKS_TO_KEEP));
+        0, m_chain.Height() + static_cast<int>(MIN_BLOCKS_TO_KEEP));
```

events.message:
test: check ActivateBestChains skips validated chainstate

catches validated chainstates being passed
to ActivateBestChains, which previously went undetected.

kills mutant https://mutanthub.space/mutants/4388

diff --git a/src/validation.cpp b/src/validation.cpp
index 6bed39ba5f..d965254192 100644
--- a/src/validation.cpp
+++ b/src/validation.cpp
@@ -6482,7 +6482,7 @@ util::Result<void> ChainstateManager::ActivateBestChains()
         LOCK(GetMutex());
         chainstates.reserve(m_chainstates.size());
         for (const auto& chainstate : m_chainstates) {
-            if (chainstate && chainstate->m_assumeutxo != Assumeutxo::INVALID && !chainstate->m_target_utxohash) {
+            if (chainstate || chainstate->m_assumeutxo != Assumeutxo::INVALID && !chainstate->m_target_utxohash) {
                 chainstates.push_back(chainstate.get());
             }
         }

test: check GetPruneRange on unvalidated snapshot

kills mutants https://mutanthub.space/mutants/4385 and
https://mutanthub.space/mutants/4386

checks prune range before a snapshot chain gets validated
ensures that pruning does not start before the snapshot block or
within the last 288 blocks.

diff --git a/src/validation.cpp b/src/validation.cpp
index 6bed39ba5f..a51e1595aa 100644
--- a/src/validation.cpp
+++ b/src/validation.cpp
@@ -6447,7 +6447,7 @@ std::pair<int, int> Chainstate::GetPruneRange(int last_height_can_prune) const
         // Only prune blocks _after_ the snapshot if this is a snapshot chain
         // that has not been fully validated yet. The earlier blocks need to be
         // kept to validate the snapshot
-        prune_start = Assert(SnapshotBase())->nHeight + 1;
+        prune_start = Assert(SnapshotBase())->nHeight - 1;
     }

     int max_prune = std::max<int>(
diff --git a/src/validation.cpp b/src/validation.cpp
index 6bed39ba5f..99238dfa73 100644
--- a/src/validation.cpp
+++ b/src/validation.cpp
@@ -6451,7 +6451,7 @@ std::pair<int, int> Chainstate::GetPruneRange(int last_height_can_prune) const
     }

     int max_prune = std::max<int>(
-        0, m_chain.Height() - static_cast<int>(MIN_BLOCKS_TO_KEEP));
+        0, m_chain.Height() + static_cast<int>(MIN_BLOCKS_TO_KEEP));

     // last block to prune is the lesser of (caller-specified height, MIN_BLOCKS_TO_KEEP from the tip)
